**Methods.** Human WT lysozyme (NP_000230.1) and *Canis lupus familiaris*
lysozyme were aligned with BLASTp ("Align two sequences", compositional
matrix adjustment), using the human sequence as the query.

**Results.** BLASTp aligned both proteins over their full length (148 aa)
with an E-value of 2e-88 (score 241 bits). There are 119 identical residues
(80 % identity) and 132 positive residues (89 % similarity), with no gaps.
Ile74 (Ile56 in the mature protein) is conserved in the dog, within the
identical motif DYGIFQ.

**Conclusion.** Conservation of Ile74 between human and dog suggests that
this position is important for the structure or function of lysozyme, so its
substitution by threonine is likely to be deleterious.
